-- The dates rejection fixture (BLAWX-EXPORT-SPEC §"Dates"): Blawx v1 rejects
-- any DATE-sorted field or argument with a named diagnostic — `dates (Blawx
-- v1)` — pointing at specs/todo/DATE-LIBRARY-SPEC.md, whose R-D1/R-D4 record
-- the eventual convention (functor-wrapped integer POSIX seconds, UTC
-- midnight). The decision below never touches the date field, so the module
-- clears the relational middle-end (the field lowers as an opaque sort with a
-- fidelity note) and the rejection is the Blawx classifier's own. No #EVAL:
-- constructing a DATE literal is beside the point, and the rejection is at
-- the declaration.

DECLARE Contract HAS
    signed IS A DATE
    amount IS A NUMBER

@export
GIVEN c IS A Contract
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is large` IF c's amount GREATER THAN 100000
